{"id": "neutrality-bare-greeting-carries-no-code-vocabulary", "key": "neutrality.bare.greeting", "note": "a bare install's greeting names the teach lane and how to seed, never a repo/index pointer", "turns": ["hi"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "^Hi\\. I'm tmct\\."}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": {"name": "answerLacks", "arg": ["--repo", "code-structure", "code graph"]}}]}
{"id": "neutrality-bare-count-declines-to-the-general-miss", "key": "neutrality.bare.count-declines-to-miss", "note": "'how many classes are there' with no code domain active is the ordinary grammar-miss wall, never '0 classes.' or a code-graph-flavored decline", "turns": ["how many classes are there"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": "isMiss"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": {"name": "answerLacks", "arg": ["classes.", "code graph"]}}]}
{"id": "neutrality-bare-code-shaped-question-declines-to-the-general-miss", "key": "neutrality.bare.code-question-declines-to-miss", "note": "a code-structure question with no code domain active is the plain grammar-miss wall, never 'no code graph is loaded' or a code-index pointer", "turns": ["which modules import a.mjs"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": "isMiss"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": {"name": "answerLacks", "arg": ["no code graph is loaded", "code index", "tmct index"]}}]}
{"id": "neutrality-bare-help-hides-the-code-domain-commands", "key": "neutrality.bare.help-hides-code-commands", "note": "/help on a bare install lists no code-graph command (/callers, /impact, /describe, /members, ...) and no counts row", "turns": ["/help"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": {"name": "answerLacks", "arg": ["/callers", "/impact", "/describe", "/members", "/find", "plus counts:"]}}]}
{"id": "neutrality-bare-orientation-carries-no-code-vocabulary", "key": "neutrality.bare.orientation-neutral", "note": "'what can you do' with no code domain active never offers --repo/tmct index/example:mini", "turns": ["what can you do"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "^I'm tmct"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": {"name": "answerLacks", "arg": ["--repo", "tmct index", "example:mini"]}}]}
{"id": "neutrality-bare-stats-reports-the-session-neutrally", "key": "neutrality.bare.stats-neutral", "note": "/stats with no code domain active reports the session's own fact count, never 'needs an index' or a graph-shaped overview", "turns": ["/stats"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "^no graph loaded — this session holds 0 facts"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": {"name": "answerLacks", "arg": ["needs an index", "entities by class"]}}]}
{"id": "neutrality-bare-capabilities-names-no-domain", "key": "neutrality.bare.capabilities-names-no-domain", "note": "/capabilities on a bare install lists the built-in tools and the taught-action state and names no loaded domain at all", "turns": ["/capabilities"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "^read-only graph tools:"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "taught actions: none yet"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": {"name": "answerLacks", "arg": ["loaded domains", "grounded by"]}}]}
{"id": "neutrality-active-greeting-offers-the-repo-pointer", "key": "neutrality.active.greeting", "note": "the code pack active (no index yet) restores today's --repo clause on the greeting", "setup": {"config": {"extensions": {"code": {"active": true}}}}, "turns": ["hi"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "^Hi\\. I'm tmct\\."}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "--repo <path>. for code-structure questions"}]}
{"id": "neutrality-active-count-answers-a-real-header-count", "key": "neutrality.active.count", "note": "the code pack active counts the graph header mechanically, even at zero, rather than declining", "setup": {"config": {"extensions": {"code": {"active": true}}}}, "turns": ["how many classes are there"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "exact", "value": "0 classes."}]}
{"id": "neutrality-active-code-question-names-the-missing-graph", "key": "neutrality.active.code-question-miss", "note": "a code-structure question with the pack active but no graph loaded yet honestly names the code domain as the reason, not a generic grammar miss", "setup": {"config": {"extensions": {"code": {"active": true}}}}, "turns": ["which modules import a.mjs"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "predicate", "value": "isMiss"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "no code graph is loaded in this session"}]}
{"id": "neutrality-active-help-shows-the-code-domain-commands", "key": "neutrality.active.help-shows-code-commands", "note": "/help with the code pack active lists the code-graph commands and the counts row, from the pack's own help rows", "setup": {"config": {"extensions": {"code": {"active": true}}}}, "turns": ["/help"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "/callers <symbol>"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "/impact <module>"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "plus counts: \"how many <classes\\|functions\\|modules\\|methods\\|commits> are there\"\\."}]}
{"id": "neutrality-active-orientation-offers-the-repo-pointer", "key": "neutrality.active.orientation-names-repo", "note": "'what can you do' with the code pack active restores today's --repo/example:mini clause", "setup": {"config": {"extensions": {"code": {"active": true}}}}, "turns": ["what can you do"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "point me at a repo: .--repo <path>., or try the shipped example .npm run example:mini."}]}
{"id": "neutrality-active-stats-shows-the-graph-overview", "key": "neutrality.active.stats-shows-graph-overview", "note": "/stats with the code pack active (no index yet) renders the graph-shaped overview, at zero, rather than the neutral fact count", "setup": {"config": {"extensions": {"code": {"active": true}}}}, "turns": ["/stats"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "^graph overview — 0 entities\\."}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "0 module\\(s\\) across 0 top-level package\\(s\\)\\."}]}
{"id": "neutrality-active-capabilities-names-the-code-domain-and-its-grounding", "key": "neutrality.active.capabilities-names-the-domain", "note": "/capabilities with the code pack active names the domain, restates the grounding channel the pack itself declares, and counts what its vocabulary adds", "setup": {"config": {"extensions": {"code": {"active": true}}}}, "turns": ["/capabilities"], "expect": [{"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "\\nloaded domains:\\n"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "code — grounded by extraction through tmct index \\(the graphPaths provider seam\\)"}, {"turn": 0, "mode": "regex", "value": "adds \\d+ commands and \\d+ count nouns"}]}
